  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I would like the Creator Guidelines to provide a clearer definition of abusive world moderation.\n\nMy concern comes from experiences with The Furry Hideout. The behavior I am reporting involves players being prevented from joining one instance and then allegedly being followed into newly created instances, where moderation action is taken against them again.\n\nWorld moderators should still be able to protect their communities and take appropriate action when necessary. However, the guidelines should clarify when repeated moderation across separate instances becomes targeted behavior rather than ordinary instance moderation.\n\nPlease clarify what moderators are permitted to do across separate instances and establish guidance against repeatedly pursuing individual players from one instance to another solely to continue restricting their access.",
